From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glm disk: carry a kept state's cuts digest in its image, so request starts resume from disk

TF_GLM_REQUEST_STARTS=1 was refused together with --learn-conversations at startup,
because a state read back from disk came back with its cuts digest zeroed: the image's
words held its position, head rows, ring bases, copy bits, world and layout, but not the
digest of its pass's chunk starts below its position (cuda_prompt_cuts.below), and
cuda_prompt_cuts.resumes refuses a state whose digest differs from the resuming pass's.
A state kept at a request start off the 2,048-row grid therefore could never be resumed,
and a grid state restored with a zero digest was refused by any pass with a cut below it.

The image's words gain a tenth word, the digest, and the format rises to 2. cuda_native's
snap_save and cuda_snapshots' keepAs record the digest in the engine's snapshot when a
state is kept; wordsOf writes it into the image; a read back decodes it and cuda_disk_ranks'
unseal sets it on the state and seals it, so the lanes' resumes check sees the digest the
image was written with. A state on the plain grid carries zero, as before. The store's
identity hashes the probe's image, words included, so a store written by the previous
build is never read: its directory differs, and decode refuses a kept file's format 1
words by name (DiskWords) rather than resuming bytes it cannot check.

This patch is new here: it is not an upstream commit, and it is written on this repo's
stack (v1.2.9, patches/pr1411, patches/cache-salt) for the GLM disk tier that pr1411
adds. It lifts the GLM startup refusal of the two settings (the TF_KV_SHARE refusal
stays) and changes the disk image's words, not its rows: the state's rows and the
resumed replies are unchanged, and a state read back has the same bytes it was saved
with.

---

